Strategy Guidance:
Design your algorithm to maintain a population of candidate solutions. At each step, balance exploration (probing new regions of the search space) and exploitation (refining the most promising solutions found so far).

Before writing code, reason through:
1. How will you balance global exploration of the search space with robust local refinement around the most promising candidates?
2. How should candidate acceptance and step sizes adapt over iterations as the evaluation budget is consumed, without making rigid assumptions about landscape smoothness or evaluation precision?
